{"id": "unknown-2026-07-13-003", "date": "2026-07-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 29, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Weekly price shock: BCI cotton- week ending July 10", "content": "China's BCI 3128B fell 0.91 per cent week-on-week (WoW) to 18,053 CNY/tonne after USDA raised 2026/27 US cotton output by 400,000 bales, erasing mid-week gains. \nIndia's Shankar-6 (₹181/kg) and Pakistan's KCA Spot (482.3 PKR/kg) were unchanged. \nIndia's duty-free import window and possible Chinese reserve auctions will steer regional cotton procurement.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/weekly-price-shock-bci-cotton-week-ending-july-10-311689-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-13-004", "date": "2026-07-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 29, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["growth", "weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India may go duty-free, but is weak in 10 of EU’s top 20 garments", "content": "India’s EU Free Trade Agreement (FTA) removes tariff barriers, but product competitiveness remains the bigger challenge.\nTexPro data show exports are still dominated by cotton apparel, while Europe’s largest opportunities lie in MMF-based jerseys and outerwear.\nExport growth will depend on broadening India’s product mix, not on duty-free access alone.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-may-go-duty-free-but-is-weak-in-10-of-eu-s-top-20-garments-311687-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-13-005", "date": "2026-07-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 29, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand", "improve"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India-EU FTA: 63% cotton basket could cap apparel export gains", "content": "India’s FTA with the EU can improve price competitiveness, but tariffs alone will not double apparel exports.\nTexPro data show India’s Europe-bound basket remains heavily cotton-focused, while demand is stronger for jerseys and outerwear.\nThe biggest opportunity lies in expanding MMF capacity and higher-value product categories before the agreement takes effect.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/india-eu-fta-63-cotton-basket-could-cap-apparel-export-gains-311684-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
